    "summary": "Prime Minister Hamza Abdi Barre laid the foundation stone for a new science and technology center in Mogadishu, aimed at advancing education and innovation.",
    "content": "Somali Prime Minister Hamza Abdi Barre laid the foundation stone for a new science and technology center in Mogadishu on [date]. The facility is intended to serve as a hub for research, innovation, and technical training in the country.\n\nThe event was attended by government officials, educators, and technology stakeholders. The center is part of broader efforts by the federal government to rebuild Somalia's educational infrastructure and promote technological advancement.\n\nThis development is significant for the Somali diaspora, which has long played a key role in the country's reconstruction through remittances and expertise. A dedicated science and technology center could create opportunities for diaspora professionals to contribute to research and innovation in Somalia.\n\nPrime Minister Barre has prioritized education and technology in his administration's agenda, emphasizing their importance for economic growth and job creation. The new center is expected to foster partnerships with international institutions and diaspora experts.\n\nFor the diaspora, this initiative signals a growing focus on knowledge-based development, potentially opening avenues for collaboration and investment in Somalia's tech sector. It also aligns with wider calls for diaspora engagement in national development.\n\nRead the original report from Horseed Media here: https://horseedmedia.net/%f0%9d%90%91%f0%9d%90%9a%f0%9d%90%a2%f0%9d%90%a2%f0%9d%90%ac%f0%9d%90%ae%f0%9d%90%a5-%f0%9d%90%96%f0%9d%90%9a%f0%9d%90%ac%f0%9d%90%9a%f0%9d%90%9a%f0%9d%90%ab%f0%9d%90%9e-%f0%9d%90%97-6/426492/",
